# Force .html paths to canonical clean paths (301 = permanent).
# Netlify's Pretty URLs feature already does this, but having an explicit
# _redirects file documents the intent in the repo and guarantees 301s
# (which is what Google needs to consolidate duplicate URLs in its index).
# The trailing ! makes the rule a forced/shadow redirect so it wins
# even if Netlify would otherwise serve the .html file directly.
/index.html         /              301!
/pricing.html       /pricing       301!
/app.html           /app           301!
/success.html       /success       301!
/for-leagues.html   /for-leagues   301!
